{#
  THE LAB SECTION'S TAB BAR, rendered by every page in the section.

  Until 2026-09-18 only `admin/lab.html.twig` called `ui.tabs`, so the four other
  destinations arrived with no tab bar at all: a tab was a one-way exit and the rail was the
  only way back, which returned you to Fleet rather than to where you were. The bar is defined
  once here so the five pages cannot drift apart.

  `active` is the label to mark, and it must match one of the labels below exactly — `ui.tabs`
  compares by label, so a typo silently marks nothing.

  The Devices tab is an EasyAdmin CRUD index with no route name of its own, so its URL comes
  from `ea_url()` rather than `path()`. That generator is a SHARED, STATEFUL service and
  `generateUrl()` does not reset it, so `unsetAll()` hands it back the way it was found.

  Two pages under /admin/lab are deliberately absent: `/admin/lab/fleet` (the standalone vitals
  page, whose table this section's Fleet tab already shows) and `/admin/lab/sessions`
  (ground-truth sessions, which are a recording, not part of what the instrument IS).
#}
{% import 'admin/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}

{% set _devices_url = ea_url().setController('App\\Controller\\Admin\\DeviceCrudController').setAction('index').generateUrl() %}
{% do ea_url().unsetAll() %}

{{ ui.tabs([
    {label: 'Fleet', href: path('admin_lab')},
    {label: 'Arming', href: path('admin_lab_arming')},
    {label: 'Devices', href: _devices_url},
    {label: 'Markers', href: path('admin_lab_placements')},
    {label: 'Bundle', href: path('admin_lab_bundle')},
], active) }}
